# Nova Schola Hub — TEST database configuration (LOCAL ONLY, never production).
#
# Copy to `.env.test` (gitignored, never committed) and point it at a dedicated,
# clearly-named test database. The test guard (src/shared/config/testGuard.js)
# enforces, before any connection is opened:
#   - NODE_ENV=test (set automatically by `npm test`)
#   - DATABASE_URL_TEST must be set (production DATABASE_URL is never used)
#   - no hosted/cloud hosts (Neon, AWS, Render, Railway, Supabase, ...)
#   - database name must contain "test"
#
# Example for a local PostgreSQL:
DATABASE_URL_TEST=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/novaschola_test?sslmode=disable
